Subject: [PATCH] axi_dw_downsizer: don't re-accept the terminal R beat (AR id-counter underflow)

Under overlapping/back-to-back reads through the wide->narrow downsizer, the read
FSM re-asserts the master-side R ready (mst_r_ready_tran[t]) in the cycle the
already-forwarded *terminal* beat (r.last) is draining to the wide slave. Because
the master valid/last is still held, the internal axi_demux id-counter is popped a
SECOND time for a single AR -> pop(2 cycles) vs push(1 cycle) -> counter 0 -> 0x3f
underflow (axi_demux_id_counters.sv cnt_underflow $fatal).

Root cause: the accept gate (line ~568) permits a new master beat whenever the
output slot is free OR being consumed, without excluding the last-beat drain. The
slot only leaves the active state one cycle later on the wide handshake (line
~638), leaving a window where the finished burst's held final beat is accepted
(and counted) again.

Fix: qualify the "output being consumed" branch of the accept gate with
!r_req_q.r.last, so once the terminal beat has been forwarded the slot stops
accepting (and stops popping) until it retires. r.last is 0 at a burst start
(so a max-size burst whose burst_len legitimately == '1 is unaffected) and 1 only
during the terminal-beat drain -- exactly the double-accept window. One
r_ready pulse per beat => one demux pop per AR push.

--- a/src/axi_dw_downsizer.sv
+++ b/src/axi_dw_downsizer.sv
@@ -563,9 +563,13 @@
           // Request was accepted
           if (!r_req_q.ar_valid) begin
             // Our turn
             if ((idqueue_id == t) && idqueue_valid) begin
-              // Ready to accept more data
-              if (!slv_r_valid_tran[t] || (slv_r_valid_tran[t] && slv_r_ready_tran[t])) begin
+              // Ready to accept more data -- but NOT while the already-forwarded
+              // terminal beat (r.last) is draining to the wide slave: re-accepting
+              // there re-pops the demux AR id-counter for a finished burst and
+              // underflows it under overlapping reads. r.last is 0 at a burst
+              // start, so a legit max burst (burst_len=='1) is unaffected.
+              if (!slv_r_valid_tran[t] ||
+                  (slv_r_valid_tran[t] && slv_r_ready_tran[t] && !r_req_q.r.last)) begin
                 mst_r_ready_tran[t] = 1'b1;

                 if (mst_resp.r_valid) begin
